        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279991",
          "text": "The weekly wages of 1000 workers are normally distributed with a mean of Rs.70 and standard deviation of Rs. 5. Estimate the number of workers whose weekly wages will be more than 80. ______<br />\n<img alt=\"GATEBOOK-2019-Probability1-1\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"/>",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "23 : 23",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1,numerical-answers",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279989",
          "text": "A die is rolled three times. The probability that exactly one odd number turns up among the three outcomes is<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $\\frac{1}{6}$<br /> </li><li>  $\\frac{3}{8}$<br /> </li> <li> $\\frac{1}{8}$<br /> </li>  <li> $\\frac{1}{2}$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279987",
          "text": "Seven coins are tossed what is the probability that the number of heads exceeds the number of tails?",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "0.45 : 0.55",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1,numerical-answers",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279986",
          "text": "Let A, B, C are independent events with probabilities $0.8, 0.5, 0.3$ respectively. The probability of occurrence of at least one of these events is _____",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "0.9 : 0.96",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1,numerical-answers",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279985",
          "text": "<p>Suppose A and B are independent events associated with an experiment. If the probability that A and&nbsp;B occurs equals $0.6$ and the probability that A occurs equals $0.6$ then the probability of B is ____</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$1$</li>\n    <li>$\\frac{2}{3}$</li>\n    <li>$0.2$</li>\n    <li>$0.5$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1,probability",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279983",
          "text": "Each of two persons, tosses three fair coins. The probability that they obtain same number of head is ____",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "0.3 : 0.32",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1,numerical-answers",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279981",
          "text": "A computer assembly consists of two sub systems, say A and B. From previous testing procedures, the following probabilities are assumed to be known.<br />\n$\\text{P(A) fails}= 0.2$<br />\n$\\text{P(B) fails alone} = 0.15$<br />\n$\\text{A and B fail} =0.15$<br />\nThen the conditional probability $\\text{P(A) fails | B has failed)} = $_____",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "0.5 : 0.5",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1,numerical-answers",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279979",
          "text": "If A, B, C are mutually exclusive and exhaustive events associated with a random experiment and $P(B) = 0.6 \\: P(A)\\text{ and }P(C) = 0.2 P(A)$ then $P(A)$ is _____<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $\\frac{1}{9}$<br /> </li><li>  $\\frac{5}{9}$<br /> </li> <li> $\\frac{7}{9}$<br /> </li>  <li> $\\frac{8}{9}$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279977",
          "text": "From a pack of well shuffled cards, one card is drawn then the probability that this card is either a king or an ace is _____<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $\\frac{1}{13}$<br /> </li><li>  $\\frac{2}{13}$<br /> </li> <li> $\\frac{7}{13}$<br /> </li>  <li> $\\frac{11}{13}$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279975",
          "text": "A bag contains 4 red and 3 black balls. A second bag contains 2 red and 4 black balls. One bag is selected at random. From the selected bag one ball is drawn, the probability that the ball drawn is red is ______",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "0.4 : 0.5",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1,numerical-answers",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279973",
          "text": "Suppose A and B are independent events associated with an experiment. If the probability that A or B occurs is $0.6$ and the probability that A occurs equals $0.4$ then the probability of B is _______<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $\\frac{1}{3}$<br /> </li><li>  $\\frac{2}{3}$<br /> </li> <li> $0.2$<br /> </li>  <li> $0.5$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279971",
          "text": "For any two events $E_1, E_2$ let $P(E_1)= \\frac{1}{2}, P(E2)=\\frac{2}{3}, P(E_1 \\cap E_2)= \\frac{1}{3}$ then $E_1, E_2$ are<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  Mutually exclusive but not independent events<br /> </li><li>  Mutually exclusive and independent events<br /> </li> <li> Independent but not mutually exclusive<br /> </li>  <li> None of these  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279969",
          "text": "A product is an assemble of $4$ different components. The product can be sequentially assembled in two possible ways. If the $4$ components are placed in a box and these are drawn at random from the box, the the probability of getting a correct sequence is _____.",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "0.082 : 0.084",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1,numerical-answers",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279967",
          "text": "A random variable $X$ has normal distribution with mean $100$. If $P(100 &lt; X &lt; 120) = \\alpha$ then $ P(X &lt; 80) =$<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $1-2 \\alpha$<br /> </li><li>  $1- \\alpha$<br /> </li> <li> $\\frac{1-2 \\alpha}{2}$<br /> </li>  <li> $\\frac{1- \\alpha}{2}$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279965",
          "text": "The number of particles emitted from a radioactive source during a specific period is a random variable with Poisson distribution. If the probability of no emissions equals $\\frac{1}{3}$, then the probability that $2$ or more emissions occur is<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $\\frac{2-\\log _e 3}{3}$<br /> </li><li>  $\\frac{3-\\log _e 2}{3}$<br /> </li> <li> $\\frac{2-\\log _e 3}{2}$<br /> </li>  <li> $\\frac{3-\\log _e 2}{3}$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279963",
          "text": "A player tosses two fair coins. He wins Rs. $2$ if $2$ heads occur and Re. $1$ if $1$ head occurs. On the other hand, he loses Rs. $3$ if no heads occur. If the player plays $100$ times, then the amount he wins is ____(Rs).",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "24.5 : 25.5",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1,numerical-answers",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279961",
          "text": "A function $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x) = \\begin{cases} 0 &amp; ; &amp; x&lt;2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{A}(2x+3) &amp; ; &amp; 2 &lt; x &lt; 4 \\\\ 0 &amp; ; &amp; x &gt;4 \\end{cases}$. For $f(x)$ to be valid probability density function the value of $A$ must be<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  8<br /> </li><li>  16<br /> </li> <li> 18<br /> </li>  <li> 22  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279959",
          "text": "If the probability of a bad reaction from a certain injection is $0.001$, then the probability that out of $2000$ individuals more than two will get a bad reaction is<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $1-\\frac{5}{e^2}$<br /> </li><li>  $1-\\frac{5}{e^3}$<br /> </li> <li> $1+\\frac{5}{e^2}$<br /> </li>  <li> $1+\\frac{5}{e^3}$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279958",
          "text": "A fair die is tossed repeatedly until a six is obtained. Let $X$ denote the number of tosses required. The probability that $X \\geq 3$ is equal to,<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $\\frac{125}{216}$<br /> </li><li>  $\\frac{25}{36}$<br /> </li> <li> $\\frac{5}{36}$<br /> </li>  <li> $\\frac{25}{216}$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279955",
          "text": "In a class $30\\%$ students like tea, $20 \\%$ like coffee and $10 \\%$ like both tea and coffee. A student is selected at random then the probability that he does not like tea if it known that he takes coffee?<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $\\frac{1}{2}$<br /> </li><li>  $\\frac{3}{4}$<br /> </li> <li> $\\frac{1}{3}$<br /> </li>  <li> $\\frac{1}{4}$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279953",
          "text": "A fair die is thrown three times and sum of the three members is found to be $16$. Find the probability that $5$ appears on the third throw.<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $\\frac{1}{2}$<br /> </li><li>  $\\frac{1}{3}$<br /> </li> <li> $\\frac{1}{4}$<br /> </li>  <li> $\\frac{1}{5}$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279951",
          "text": "If $A$ and $B$ are two events such that $P(A)=0.4$ and $P(A \\cup \\bar{B})=0.7$. If $A$ and $B$ are independent events, then $P(B)$ is ____<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $0.5$<br /> </li><li>  $0.4$<br /> </li> <li> $0.6$<br /> </li>  <li> $0.3$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279949",
          "text": "The probability of that at least one of the events $A$ and $B$ occurs is $0.8$ and the probability that both the events occur simultaneously is $0.25$ then the probability $P(\\bar{A})+P(\\bar{B})$ is _____",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "0.94 : 0.96",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1,numerical-answers",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "279947",
          "text": "Two dice are tossed oncem the probability of getting an even number on the first dice or a total of $8$ is ____<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $\\frac{2}{9}$<br /> </li><li>  $\\frac{5}{9}$<br /> </li> <li> $\\frac{3}{2}$<br /> </li>  <li> $\\frac{1}{2}$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-probability1",
          "category": "Probability"
        }
      ]
